{"created": "2026-08-05T11:26:08.393081+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-05T11:26:08.953740+00:00", "id": 21806398, "conceptrecid": "21806397", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21806397", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "metadata": {"title": "A Degree-Spread Bound Between Independent Domination and Minimum Maximal Matchings: A Conjecture", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "publication_date": "2026-08-05", "description": "<p>For a finite simple graph G, let i(G) be its independent domination number, let mu*(G) be the minimum cardinality of a maximal matching, and let Delta(G) and delta(G) be its maximum and minimum degrees. We conjecture that every connected nontrivial graph satisfies i(G)-mu*(G) &lt;= Delta(G)-delta(G). For regular graphs this specializes to the open TxGraffiti conjecture i(G) &lt;= mu*(G). The correction by degree spread is best possible: equality holds for every balanced double star. Connectedness and nontriviality are necessary. We report exhaustive verification for all 273,192 connected nonisomorphic graphs of orders 2 through 9, together with supplementary structured and random tests. These finite computations are evidence only and do not constitute a proof.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Achour, Hassine", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher"}], "keywords": ["independent domination", "minimum maximal matching", "edge domination", "saturation number", "degree spread", "graph theory", "combinatorics"], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21806397"}}]}, "notes": "Conjectural research note with exact finite computational evidence; no proof is claimed."}, "title": "A Degree-Spread Bound Between Independent Domination and Minimum Maximal Matchings: A Conjecture", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21806398", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21806398?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21806398", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806397", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21806397", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21806397", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21806397", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21806398:paper.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21806398/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21806398/access/users", "access_request"